{"findings":["minidb/planner.py: `build_sources` reads `self.select.from_table` directly while every other node access is defensive (`getattr(join, 'kind', 'INNER')`, `alias_of`); nodes.py declares the FROM field of Select, and if it is named `from_`/`table`/`source` this raises AttributeError on every query -> agree the field name with nodes.py and read it through the same defensive helper used for joins.","minidb/planner.py: `plan()` has no catch-all, so an AttributeError/TypeError from an unexpected node shape escapes a module whose contract is QueryError-only (api.py then reports every query as an internal error) -> wrap the body of plan() in `except QueryError: raise` / `except Exception as exc: raise QueryError(...) from exc`.","minidb/planner.py: `validate` only unpacks a BinOp right operand when it is a `tuple`; if the IN list arrives as a wrapper node (e.g. Func('IN_LIST', [...]) or a list) it falls into the Func branch and is rejected as an unknown function, so `x IN (1, 2)` fails -> recognise the IN-list container explicitly and validate its elements as ordinary expressions.","minidb/planner.py: `build_sources` iterates every row of every table to build `known`, contradicting the planner's published promise that it reads only the first row for column order, and it makes columns that appear only in later rows bindable while `*` still omits them -> derive both `known` and `ordered` from the first row only.","minidb/planner.py: `open_schema` makes any column name bind against a zero-row table, so `SELECT nosuch FROM empty_t` yields NULL instead of the QueryError the spec requires for an unknown column; with two empty sources it reports ambiguity for a name that exists nowhere -> resolve against real sources first and raise `unknown column` when no source declares the name.","minidb/engine.py: `_select_items`/`_expand_star`/`_output_name` re-do Star expansion and output naming, which the planner's contract says is already done (`plan.select_items` never contains Star and carries final `name`); two implementations of the naming rules will drift -> consume PlannedItem.name/expr only and drop the star/naming code.","minidb/engine.py: the dedupe in `_select_items` (`ordered = [pair for pair in ordered if pair[0] != name]`) applies to the whole select list, not just `*` expansion, so `SELECT a AS x, b AS x FROM t` silently loses the first column; the later-wins rule is specified only for `*` collisions -> restrict the dedupe to star-expanded columns.","minidb/engine.py: `_join_conditions` pads missing ON conditions with None and `_field(plan, (..., 'joins', ...))` may pick up a Join list rather than conditions; a None condition becomes an unconditional cross product, which INNER JOIN never is -> read `plan.join_conditions` only and raise QueryError when its length is not len(sources) - 1.","minidb/engine.py: `_field`/`_source_entry`/`_descending` guess attribute names ('where_clause', 'filter', 'is_distinct', 'position', 'desc', ...) that the Plan interface does not publish; whichever attribute happens to exist first wins, so a rename in planner.py silently changes behaviour instead of failing -> read the published Plan/PlannedItem/PlannedOrderKey fields directly.","minidb/engine.py: the listing is truncated before `_run`, `_eval`, the aggregate evaluation and the negative LIMIT/OFFSET check, so DISTINCT-before-ORDER-BY, three-valued logic, NULL-first/last ordering, mixed-type comparison raising QueryError, COUNT(*) counting rows including all-NULL ones, AVG returning float, and the SCALARS(*args) vs AGGREGATES(list) calling conventions could not be verified -> re-send the remainder of the file for review."],"target":"minidb/planner.py, minidb/engine.py (reviewed from minidb/api.py)"}